UnitPoolFactory::constructor
├── when the implementation is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the pool admin is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the pauser is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the fee manager is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the discount registry manager is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the pool tape manager is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the factory registry is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
└── given a freshly deployed factory
    ├── it should emit SetPoolAdmin
    ├── it should emit SetPauser
    ├── it should emit SetFeeManager
    ├── it should emit SetPoolTapeManager
    ├── it should emit SetDefaultFee
    ├── it should set implementation to the variant pool implementation
    ├── it should set poolAdmin to the provided pool admin
    ├── it should set pauser to the provided pauser
    ├── it should set feeManager to the provided fee manager
    ├── it should set defaultFee to the variant default fee
    ├── it should set poolTapeManager to the provided pool tape manager
    └── it should set factoryRegistry to the provided factory registry

UnitPoolFactory::setPoolAdmin
├── when the caller is not the pool admin
│   └── it should revert with NotPoolAdmin
└── when the caller is the pool admin
    ├── when the new admin is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new admin is not the zero address
        ├── it should update poolAdmin
        └── it should emit SetPoolAdmin

UnitPoolFactory::setPauser
├── when the caller is not the pauser
│   └── it should revert with NotPauser
└── when the caller is the pauser
    ├── when the new pauser is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new pauser is not the zero address
        ├── it should update pauser
        └── it should emit SetPauser

UnitPoolFactory::setPauseState
├── when the caller is not the pauser
│   └── it should revert with NotPauser
└── when the caller is the pauser
    ├── when the new state is true
    │   ├── it should update isPaused to true
    │   └── it should emit SetPauseState
    └── when the new state is false
        ├── it should update isPaused to false
        └── it should emit SetPauseState

UnitPoolFactory::setFeeManager
├── when the caller is not the fee manager
│   └── it should revert with NotFeeManager
└── when the caller is the fee manager
    ├── when the new fee manager is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new fee manager is not the zero address
        ├── it should update feeManager
        └── it should emit SetFeeManager

UnitPoolFactory::setFeeModule
├── when the caller is not the fee manager
│   └── it should revert with NotFeeManager
└── when the caller is the fee manager
    ├── when the new fee module is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new fee module is not the zero address
        ├── when the gas limit is zero
        │   └── it should revert with ZeroGasLimit
        └── when the gas limit is gt zero
            ├── when the new fee module is bound to a different factory
            │   └── it should revert with InvalidFeeModule
            └── when the new fee module is bound to this factory
                ├── it should update feeModule
                ├── it should update feeModuleGasLimit
                └── it should emit SetFeeModule

UnitPoolFactory::setDefaultFee
├── when the caller is not the fee manager
│   └── it should revert with NotFeeManager
└── when the caller is the fee manager
    ├── when the new fee is zero
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroFee
    └── when the new fee is greater than zero
        ├── when the new fee is greater than the max fee
        │   └── it should revert with FeeTooHigh
        └── when the new fee is less than the max fee
            ├── it should update defaultFee
            └── it should emit SetDefaultFee

UnitPoolFactory::createPool
├── when tokenA equals tokenB
│   └── it should revert with SameAddress
└── when tokenA differs from tokenB
    ├── when the lower token is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the lower token is not the zero address
        ├── when the pool already exists for the pair
        │   └── it should revert with PoolAlreadyExists
        └── when the pair has no pool yet
            ├── it should deploy a clone at the predicted deterministic address
            ├── it should initialize the pool with the sorted token pair
            ├── it should store the pool in the mapping in both directions
            ├── it should append the pool to allPools
            ├── it should mark the pool as a valid pool in _isPools mapping
            ├── it should push pool keyed by tokenA to poolByTokenIndex
            ├── it should push pool keyed by tokenB to poolByTokenIndex
            ├── it should push pool and timestamp to poolsIndex
            ├── it should add tokenA to tokenIndex
            ├── it should add tokenB to tokenIndex
            ├── it should register the pool as a target in the factory registry
            ├── it should emit PoolCreated
            └── when the factory registry reverts the registration
                └── it should revert

UnitPoolFactory::getBaseFee
├── when no fee module is set
│   └── it should return the default fee
└── when a fee module is set
    ├── when there isn't enough gas left for the external call
    │   └── it should revert with InsufficientGasForCall
    └── when there is enough gas left for the external call
        ├── when the fee module call reverts
        │   └── it should return the default fee
        ├── when the fee module returns a fee above the custom cap
        │   └── it should return the default fee
        └── when the fee module returns a fee within the custom cap
            └── it should return the custom fee

UnitPoolFactory::setDiscountRegistryManager
├── when the caller is not the discount registry manager
│   └── it should revert with NotDiscountRegistryManager
└── when the caller is the discount registry manager
    ├── when the new discount registry manager is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new discount registry manager is not the zero address
        ├── it should update discountRegistryManager
        └── it should emit SetDiscountRegistryManager

UnitPoolFactory::setDiscountRegistry
├── when the caller is not the discount registry manager
│   └── it should revert with NotDiscountRegistryManager
└── when the caller is the discount registry manager
    ├── when the new discount registry is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new discount registry is not the zero address
        ├── it should update discountRegistry
        └── it should emit SetDiscountRegistry

UnitPoolFactory::setPoolTapeManager
├── when the caller is not the pool tape manager
│   └── it should revert with NotPoolTapeManager
└── when the caller is the pool tape manager
    ├── when the new manager is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new manager is not the zero address
        ├── it should update poolTapeManager
        └── it should emit SetPoolTapeManager

UnitPoolFactory::setPoolTape
├── when the caller is not the pool tape manager
│   └── it should revert with NotPoolTapeManager
└── when the caller is the pool tape manager
    ├── when the gas limit is zero
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroGasLimit
    └── when the gas limit is gt zero
        ├── it should update poolTape
        ├── it should update poolTapeGasLimit
        └── it should emit SetPoolTape

UnitPoolFactory::recordPoolTape
├── when no pool tape is set
│   └── it should not record the swap data into a pool tape
└── when a pool tape is set
    ├── when the caller is not a pool
    │   └── it should not forward to the pool tape
    └── when the caller is a pool
        ├── when there isn't enough gas left for the external call
        │   └── it should revert with InsufficientGasForCall
        └── when there is enough gas left for the external call
            └── it should forward the pool's record data to the pool tape

UnitPoolFactory::setMevTaxModule
├── when the caller is not the fee manager
│   └── it should revert with NotFeeManager
└── when the caller is the fee manager
    ├── when the gas limit is zero
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroGasLimit
    └── when the gas limit is gt zero
        ├── when the new mev tax module is the zero address
        │   ├── it should clear mevTaxModule
        │   └── it should emit SetMevTaxModule
        └── when the new mev tax module is not the zero address
            ├── it should update mevTaxModule
            ├── it should update mevTaxModuleGasLimit
            └── it should emit SetMevTaxModule

UnitPoolFactory::getFee
├── when no mev tax module is set
│   └── it should return the base fee with zero mev fee and false toxic
└── when a mev tax module is set
    ├── when there isn't enough gas left for the external call
    │   └── it should revert with InsufficientGasForCall
    └── when there is enough gas left for the external call
        ├── it should forward the pool to the module
        ├── when the module call fails
        │   └── it should return the base fee with zero mev fee and false toxic
        └── when the module call succeeds
            ├── when the module returns a tax above the maximum encodable tax
            │   └── it should return the base fee with zero mev fee and false toxic
            ├── when the module returns a valid tax and toxic flag
            │   ├── it should return the base fee plus the mev fee in bps
            │   ├── it should return the mev fee in bps
            │   └── it should return the toxic boolean
            └── when fee plus mev is higher than MAX_FEE
                ├── it should return MAX_FEE
                └── it should return the mev fee clamped to the remainder

UnitPoolFactory::setExactOutFeeQuoter
├── when the caller is not the fee manager
│   └── it should revert with NotFeeManager
└── when the caller is the fee manager
    ├── when the new quoter is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new quoter is not the zero address
        ├── when the new quoter is bound to a different factory
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidExactOutFeeQuoter
        └── when the new quoter is bound to this factory
            ├── it should update exactOutFeeQuoter
            └── it should emit SetExactOutFeeQuoter

UnitPoolFactory::getFeeForAmountIn
├── when no exact out fee quoter is set
│   └── it should revert with NoExactOutFeeQuoter
└── when an exact out fee quoter is set
    ├── when the quoter reverts
    │   └── it revert
    ├── when the quoter returns a fee above the max fee
    │   └── it should revert with FeeTooHigh
    └── when the quoter returns a fee within the max fee
        ├── it should forward the pool caller amounts and reserves to the quoter
        └── it should return the quoted fee
